;; RING-PIPELINED MMA gradients — numeric proof (138/04 and 138/05's structure, on BMG).
;;
;; Deliberately the PIPELINED TWIN of spec 09: same Mt/Nt/Kt, same ramp, same expected gradient,
;; differing in exactly one thing — the operands are slots of a RING refilled inside the K-loop
;; rather than two tiles staged once.  That isolates ring pipelining as the single variable.
;;
;; WHY THIS SPEC EXISTS — AND WHY IT IS CURRENTLY SKIPPED.  138/04 and 138/05 are the payoff
;; kernels of Chapter 2, and both are sm_90a PTX, so no NVIDIA backward can be driven
;; numerically (VERIFY-AUTODIFF has only :l0 and :opencl runtimes).  Un-skipping them on "it
;; compiles" would be the 135/01 mistake — that one compiled, had the right atomics, and
;; returned exactly 0.0.  This spec was written to supply the missing numeric proof on hardware
;; we can actually run.
;;
;; It cannot yet do so.  Writing it turned up BUG 040: MMA reading from a RING SLOT is wrong in
;; the FORWARD on BMG (metal MMA_WRONG, C[0][1]=18 against a reference of 30), reproduced at
;; HEAD with no AD change in play.  So the finite difference here reads 0.0 for a reason that
;; has nothing to do with gradients, and 138/04-05 stay skipped: their AD side now RESOLVES,
;; but resolving is not the same as being right, and nothing yet demonstrates that it is.
;; The spec is kept, ready, with the correct expectation already in place.
;;
;; WHAT WAS WRONG, and it was a mistake about MEANING rather than a missing feature.  The kernel
;; computes C = A.B.  The ring, the prologue and the prefetch are SCHEDULE; reverse-mode AD is
;; determined by the function, not by how operands were staged, so any correct matmul backward
;; pairs with this forward.  The VJP nevertheless declined, because it asked
;;
;;     "which load site filled this slot?"
;;
;; — a question about the schedule, which genuinely has two answers (the prologue's and the
;; prefetch's, with different origins), so it looked ambiguous and I recorded it as a hard trap.
;; The question the derivative actually needs is
;;
;;     "what global matrix does this operand DENOTE, and at what tile coordinate is it CONSUMED?"
;;
;; Both have exactly one answer: A-ring is only ever loaded from A, and the consumption
;; coordinate is the enclosing K-loop's, which the backward already mirrors.  The prefetch origin
;; the objection was built on belongs to a DIFFERENT PIPELINE STAGE than the one being read.
;;
;; Only the PRIMAL needed fixing.  The adjoint flow was already correct: reversing the pipeline
;; scatters a slot's adjoint at the prefetch's origin next-k, and the slot consumed at iteration
;; k is exactly the one the prefetch of iteration k-2 wrote with next-k = k, so the mirror lands
;; on the right stage by construction.
;;
;; THE CHECK.  f(A,B) = sum(A.B), so dA[m,k] = sum_n B[k,n].  With B[i][j] = 0.01*(i*16+j),
;; dA[1,0] = 0.01 * (0+1+...+15) = 1.2 — identical to spec 09, so any divergence between the two
;; is attributable to the ring alone.  K=48 over a 2-deep ring is THREE K-steps, the smallest
;; shape where the ring actually WRAPS (with two steps the prologue would cover everything and
;; nothing would be prefetched — the pipelining would be untested).
;;
;; atol is loose for the same reason as 09: tf32's ~10-bit mantissa on both the FD and the
;; MMA-computed analytical gradient.
;;
;; COMPILE-WITH[--hardware-profile=bmg --ir-target=spv]: PASS
;; SKIP-DEFAULT-PASS
;; SKIP-WITH[--debug]: "pre-existing --debug c-t-accessor codegen bug (plan/bugs.md #033)"
;; HOIST-HARDWARE-PROFILE: bmg
;; SKIP-WITH[--differentiate]: "BUG 044: the ring-pipelined BACKWARD is wrong on BMG -- analytical reads 84.32 against an expected 1.2, while the finite difference reads 1.1992 (correct). BUG 040 is FIXED (2026-08-14) and was NOT what blocked this: fixing it moved neither number, because this spec's FD perturbs A[1,0], which lies entirely inside K-step 0 and so was always blind to 040's truncation. The forward is now independently proven by 138/07 and 138/08 (MMA_CORRECT on metal, slot 0 and slot 1). The expectation below is already the right one; un-skip when 044 is fixed."
;; VERIFY-AUTODIFF: A=8x48@0:0.01 B=48x16@0:0.01 at.A=1,0 group=16 h=0.5 atol=2e-2 expect.A=1.2 output-mat=8x16

(def-hardware-profile bmg :simd-width 16 :mma-shapes ((8 16 8)))

(def-type a-mat (matrix float :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))
(def-type b-mat (matrix float :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))
(def-type c-mat (matrix float :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))

(def-kernel ring_pipelined_matmul (A B &out C)
  (declare #'(a-mat b-mat &out c-mat)
           (global-size :set-to 16)
           (local-size  :set-to 16))
  (let ((A-ring (make-scratch-matrix-ring float (8 16)  :ring-count 2))   ; Mt x Kt per slot
        (B-ring (make-scratch-matrix-ring float (16 16) :ring-count 2))   ; Kt x Nt per slot
        (C-tile (make-register-tile float (8 16) 0.0))
        (K      (inner-dimension A B)))
    ;; PROLOGUE — fill both slots before any math, so the loop always consumes a full slot.
    (dotimes (i 2)
      (load-tile A (ring-get A-ring (to-ulong i)) (0 (to-ulong i)))
      (load-tile B (ring-get B-ring (to-ulong i)) ((to-ulong i) 0)))
    ;; MAIN K-LOOP — consume slot k, then refill it for stage k+2 (the ring WRAPS).
    (dotimes (grid-k (/ (to-ulong K) (to-ulong 16)))
      (let ((slot (mod grid-k (to-ulong 2))))
        (sync-workgroup)
        (mma-accumulate-via-tile (8 16 8) C-tile (ring-get A-ring slot) (ring-get B-ring slot))
        ;; Every thread must be done reading this slot before the refill overwrites it.
        (sync-workgroup)
        (let ((next-k (+ grid-k (to-ulong 2))))
          (let ((more-k? (to-workgroup-uniform (< next-k (/ (to-ulong K) (to-ulong 16))))))
            (when more-k?
              (load-tile A (ring-get A-ring slot) (0 next-k))
              (load-tile B (ring-get B-ring slot) (next-k 0)))))))
    (store-tile C-tile C (0 0))))
